{
  "basis": "The dashboard (chart_1) presents two conflicting encodings of 'Reported reduction share (%)'. The printed data labels are 41.2% (Building retrofits), 29.8% (Transit electrification), 18.5% (Industrial efficiency), 7.2% (Tree canopy), and 3.3% (Methane capture). The bar heights are approximately 40, 68, 52, 22, and 35 respectively. The printed labels sum to 100% (41.2 + 29.8 + 18.5 + 7.2 + 3.3 = 100.0), which confirms they represent the complete share distribution for the portfolio. In contrast, the bar heights sum to approximately 217, which is not a valid share distribution. Therefore, the printed labels are the authoritative values for contribution share. The largest printed value is 41.2% for Building retrofits.",
  "option_label": "Route Building retrofits to accelerated program review"
}
